### 2. Phone Model Scanner
**File to create: `src/services/localModelScanner.ts`**

This scans for available on-device models. For the PWA path, it uses the **Web File System Access API** to let the user point to a downloaded `.task` file. For native, it scans `/sdcard/Android/data/com.google.ai.edge.gallery/` where Edge Gallery caches model files: [ai.google](https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/integrations/mobile)

```typescript
export interface LocalModelInfo {
  name: string;
  path: string;         // OPFS handle or native path
  sizeGB: number;
  source: 'edge_gallery' | 'manual';
  isLoaded: boolean;
}

export async function scanForLocalModels(): Promise<LocalModelInfo[]>
```

The scan result feeds a new `'model'` view in `ViewMode`  that shows detected models with load/unload controls.

***

### 3. MediaPipe Web LLM Integration
**Install: `npm install @mediapipe/tasks-genai`**

The MediaPipe web package  runs on WebGPU in Chrome on Android. Once the user picks a `.task` model file: [ai.google](https://ai.google.dev/edge/mediapipe/solutions/genai/llm_inference)

```typescript
import { LlmInference } from '@mediapipe/tasks-genai';

const llm = await LlmInference.createFromOptions(wasmFileset, {
  baseOptions: { modelAssetPath: modelUrl },
  maxTokens: 512,
  topK: 40,
  temperature: 0.8,
});

const result = await llm.generateResponse(prompt);
```

This becomes your `GemmaWebProvider` implementation and directly replaces the Gemini SDK for on-device calls.

***

### 4. Capacitor Wrapper for Native Access
**Install: `npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/android`**

Run `npx cap init` and `npx cap add android`. This converts the existing Vite PWA into a native Android app with zero code rewrite. Then add a Capacitor plugin that: [developers.googleblog](https://developers.googleblog.com/on-device-function-calling-in-google-ai-edge-gallery/)
- Calls the Android MediaPipe `LlmInference` SDK directly
- Reads Edge Gallery's model directory via `ContentResolver`
- Returns streaming tokens back to the web layer via `notifyListeners`

This is what gives you parity with Edge Gallery's actual runtime, not just the web approximation.

